# //// Neoffice — commit-the-build. Upstream ignores the vite output
# //// (crm/public/frontend + crm/www/crm.html) and expects every instance to
# //// run `bench build`; our fleet runs on 2-vCPU client VMs where that build
# //// is the slowest step of an update, so the two ignores below are commented
# //// out and the artifacts are committed (by hand, or by build-frontend.yml).
# //// Same reason for the CLAUDE.md line further down: it was ignored between
# //// 311c355b and c29f98c6, then shipped again. Commits d7c4209b / f5abf846 /
# //// c29f98c6. Re-ignore them only if the fleet goes back to building on the
# //// instances.
# 2026-05-07 (NORA #28) — build outputs are committed on this branch.
# See docs/COMMIT-BUILD-PATTERN.md in neoffice-devops.
# crm/public/frontend
# crm/www/crm.html
build
# CLAUDE.md  # 2026-05-07 unshipped to document commit-the-build pipeline
# //// Neoffice — never commit a compiled catalogue again. Frappe reads MO files
# //// only from <bench>/sites/assets/locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/<app>.mo
# //// (frappe/gettext/translate.py: get_translations_from_mo -> get_locale_dir),
# //// which `bench build` and `bench compile-po-to-mo` generate on the instance.
# //// A .mo inside the app is therefore never read: the one we shipped until
# //// 2026-09-04 had drifted to 877 entries against 1338 in fr.po and made a
# //// reader believe ~460 French strings were lost. The PO is the source.
crm/locale/*.mo
